<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes:   1 These results have been prepared in accordance with the recognition and measurement principles laid down in Indian Accounting Standards notified under section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013. These results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee and upon their recommendation, approved by the BOD at their meeting held on 23 Jan 2025. The Statutory auditors of the Company have carried out the limited review of the financial results for the quarter and 09 months ended 31 Dec 24 and an unmodified review report has been issued.    2. The consolidated financial results are prepared in accordance with IndAS-110 as specified under the section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013.   4. On 31 Aug 23, the Company had acquired 65% of the shares held by the shareholders of each entity of Liberate Group i.e. Liberate Learning Pty Ltd (Australia), Liberate eLearning Pty Ltd (Australia), App-eLearn Pty Ltd (Australia), and Liberate Learning Limited (New Zealand) through MPS Interactive Systems Limited, for a consideration of AUD 9.32million. The consideration of AUD 7.58Million due at completion was paid upon acquisition and the remaining amount will be paid at a later date as per the terms of the Share Purchase Agreement and other transaction documents dated 29 Aug 23 and 31 Aug 23. The consideration of AUD 9.32million has been revised to AUD 9.10 million post net working capital adjustments carried out in accordance with the SPA. The remaining 35% shareholding of Liberate Group will be acquired in subsequent tranches based upon valuation methodology as agreed under the transaction documents and liability of the same has been recognized in the financial statements. Liberate Learning Limited (New Zealand) was voluntarily dissolved and ceased to be a step-down subsidiary effective from 07 Nov 24.   5.On 29 Feb 24, the Company completed the acquisition of American Journal Experts LLC, NC, USA along with its subsidiary American Journal Online (Beijing) Information Consulting Limited, Beijing, China, AI-Tool and Research Quality Evaluation from Springer Science+Business Media LLC a Subsidiary of Springer Nature Group, through a newly formed Special Purpose Vehicle American Journal Experts LLC, under MPS North America LLC, total purchase consideration of USD 8.40Million paid as per the terms of Membership Interest Purchase Agreement and other transaction documents.   This being a Business Combination, thus based on the preliminary purchase price allocation to the various identifiable acquired assets and assumed liabilities, the provisional goodwill of INR 74crores has been recognized. Company has granted a loan of USD 3.6Million to MPS North America LLC to fund acquisition.   6. The NRC at its meeting held on 27 Sept 24, considered and approved the 2nd grant of 1,10,970 options to the eligible employees of the Holding Company and its subsidiary under ‘MPS Limited- ESOS 2023’. These options were subsequently granted to eligible employees of Holding Company and its subsidiary.    7. BOD in their meeting on 21 May 24 recommended final dividend of INR 45per equity share for FY 23-24, approved by shareholders in AGM held on 08 Aug 24 and has been paid.    8. BOD in their meeting held on 23 Jan 25 declared an Interim dividend of INR 33per equity share for FY 24-25.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
